                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Stomatology B aims to cultivate students' understanding of the basic anatomy and physiology of the oral and maxillofacial region, as well as the clinical manifestations and treatment principles of common oral internal and surgical diseases. Through the study of this course, students will be able to make preliminary diagnoses of common oral diseases and propose reasonable treatment recommendations. Meanwhile, it focuses on developing students' critical thinking, self-learning abilities, and clinical and research thinking skills, providing essential professional knowledge for future clinical and forensic practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
